{
  "_meta": {
    "purpose": "Resolves D-9. OpenEMR/Synthea lab results carry no reference ranges or abnormal flags (DQ-2), so the co-pilot applies this documented fallback table to classify abnormality deterministically. LOINC-keyed, unit-checked, sex/age-aware.",
    "sourcing_policy": "These are conventional adult reference intervals drawn from widely published clinical-chemistry consensus (Mayo/ARUP-style adult ranges). Reference intervals are properly the property of the PERFORMING laboratory and instrument; in production these MUST be replaced by the reporting lab's own ranges when the source system provides them. This table is a documented fallback, applied only when the source omits ranges, and it is the single audited place where an abnormality decision can be traced.",
    "pediatric_policy": "Adult ranges are not valid for patients under 18. When age < 18 the classifier returns no_range rather than applying an adult interval.",
    "unit_policy": "A value is classified only if the result unit matches the table unit (case/space-insensitive). A unit mismatch returns unit_mismatch and the value is left unclassified.",
    "version": "2026-07-31"
  },
  "analytes": {
